Important query types:

- pair compatibility cache;
- inherited method candidate cache;
- overridden targets cache;
- common concrete implementation cache.

## OverloadSetOracle

The overload-set oracle builds sets on demand:

```cpp
class OverloadSetOracle {
public:
    const OverloadSet &GetOverloadSet(const OverloadSetKey &key);
    const OverloadSet &ExpandExplicitOverload(ir::OverloadDeclaration *decl);
    void Clear();
};
```

Overload sets should generally be lazy because most possible member-name/type combinations are never used.

## Generic substitution context matters

A cache key must not be only:

```cpp
{ baseSignaturePointer, derivedSignaturePointer }
```

because inherited generic signatures may need to be viewed through a derived instantiation.

Example:

```ts
class B<T extends Object> {
    foo(p: T) {}
}

class D extends B<string> {
    foo(p: string) {}
}
```

The oracle should model inherited candidates as:

```cpp
struct InheritedMethodCandidate {
    Signature *originalSignature; // declaration signature
    Signature *viewSignature;     // substituted as seen from derived type
    ETSObjectType *declaringType;
    ETSObjectType *viewOwner;
};
```

Then relation checks use the correct view signature and context.

