## Phase 1: classify suppressed overriding failures by semantic service

Do not treat the default-interface case as a one-off patch. There are many nearby suppressed tests, so this phase should map failures to the relation service that must own them:

- duplicate override-of-same-base diagnostics → `OverrideOracle`;
- class/superclass implementation dominance → `OverrideOracle` + `DefaultImplementationResolver`;
- subinterface default overriding superinterface default → `DefaultImplementationResolver` using `OverrideOracle` dominance;
- inherited superclass-selected defaults → `DefaultImplementationResolver`;
- generic default/override views → `GenericViewResolver` used by all relation services;
- verifier-safe default/bridge emission → default resolver + bridge planner consumers.

The outcome should be a test/bug-family matrix and a set of shared query APIs, not a collection of local conditionals.

