Example usage: class/interface validation should resolve default conflicts before reporting `ESE0187`:

```cpp
void ValidateInterfaceDefaultPair(ETSObjectType *classType, Signature *sigA, Signature *sigB)
{
    auto &defaults = checker->SemanticRelations().DefaultImplementations();

    if (defaults.HasCommonImplementation(classType, sigA, sigB)) {
        return; // one class/superclass/default implementation resolves both requirements
    }

    auto a = defaults.ResolveImplementation(classType, sigA);
    auto b = defaults.ResolveImplementation(classType, sigB);
    if (a.IsConflict() || b.IsConflict() || !a.IsSameImplementation(b)) {
        LogInterfaceDefaultConflict(classType, sigA, sigB);
    }
}
```

Example usage: lowering/emission should consume the selected implementation instead of letting verifier discover conflicts:

```cpp
auto resolution = checker->SemanticRelations().DefaultImplementations().ResolveImplementation(classType, requirement);

if (resolution.IsSelectedInterfaceDefault()) {
    EmitDefaultForwarder(classType, resolution.Target());
} else if (resolution.IsConflict()) {
    ES2PANDA_UNREACHABLE(); // checker should already have reported the diagnostic
}
```

