edits.newText:
Overload sets should generally be lazy because most possible member-name/type combinations are never used. A call expression asks for one overload set, validates candidates against its arguments, and stores the selected target. The cache is discarded on `Recheck` or plugin mutation barriers.

Example usage: method-call resolution asks the oracle for the ordered candidate set, then stores the selected target on the call expression:

```cpp
void ResolveInstanceCall(ir::CallExpression *call, ETSObjectType *receiverType, util::StringView name)
{
    auto &overloads = checker->SemanticRelations().Overloads();
    const auto &set = overloads.GetOverloadSet({
        .receiverType = receiverType,
        .scope = nullptr,
        .name = name,
        .kind = OverloadSetKind::INSTANCE_METHOD,
    });

    auto selected = ResolveFirstApplicable(set, call->Arguments(), call->TypeParams());
    call->SetSignature(selected.signature);
    call->SetResolvedCallTarget(selected.ToCallTarget());
}
```

Example usage: explicit overload validation expands listed implicit overload groups through the same service:

```cpp
const auto &expanded = checker->SemanticRelations().Overloads().ExpandExplicitOverload(overloadDecl);
CheckExplicitOverloadExportRules(overloadDecl, expanded);
```

