    <h2>Default implementation rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Prefer concrete class/superclass methods when they override the interface requirement.</li>
      <li>Collect applicable interface defaults only when no class implementation exists.</li>
      <li>Remove defaults overridden by more specific subinterface defaults.</li>
      <li>Preserve a superclass-selected default as inherited implementation when appropriate.</li>
      <li>Use substituted generic interface views for parameterized defaults.</li>
      <li>Feed the selected implementation to lowering/emission so the verifier does not see multiple unresolved defaults.</li>
    </ul>
