    <pre><code>// Usage: method-call resolution
const auto &set = overloads.GetOverloadSet({receiverType, nullptr,
                                            name,
                                            OverloadSetKind::INSTANCE_METHOD});
auto selected = ResolveFirstApplicable(set, call-&gt;Arguments(), call-&gt;TypeParams());
call-&gt;SetSignature(selected.signature);
call-&gt;SetResolvedCallTarget(selected.ToCallTarget());</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="kicker">Generics-specific design</div>
    <h2>Inherited generic signatures are viewpoint-dependent</h2>
    <p>Generics are not a corner case for this feature. Override and overload answers for inherited generic methods depend on how a generic supertype is instantiated by the current derived type.</p>
    <pre><code>class B&lt;T extends Object&gt; {
    foo(p: T): T { return p }
}

class D extends B&lt;string&gt; {
    override foo(p: string): string { return p }
}</code></pre>
    <div class="grid three">
      <div class="box"><h3>Original</h3><p><code>B.foo(T): T</code></p></div>
      <div class="box"><h3>View from D</h3><p><code>B.foo(string): string</code></p></div>
      <div class="box"><h3>Runtime/erased</h3><p>Descriptor based on effective or erased types; may require a bridge.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="kicker">Generics-specific design</div>
    <h2>GenericViewResolver</h2>
    <pre><code>class GenericViewResolver {
public:
    Signature *ViewSignatureFrom(ETSObjectType *derivedType,
                                 ETSObjectType *declaringType,
                                 Signature *signature);

    ETSObjectType *ViewTypeFrom(ETSObjectType *derivedType,
                                ETSObjectType *declaringType);
};</code></pre>
    <ul>
      <li><code>OverrideOracle</code> compares derived methods against inherited <em>view signatures</em>, not always original declaration signatures.</li>
      <li><code>OverloadSetOracle</code> adds inherited generic candidates using the correct receiver-type view.</li>
      <li><code>DefaultImplementationResolver</code> resolves parameterized interface defaults using the correct substituted view.</li>
      <li>Bridge generation uses the same view signature to decide whether a runtime adapter is needed.</li>
      <li>Substituted signature views should be cached until <code>Recheck</code> or plugin cache clear.</li>
      <li>Generic type-parameter constraint variance needs a consistent rule; clarify spec wording if needed.</li>
    </ul>
    <pre><code>// Usage: compare derived method with inherited generic view
Signature *baseView = genericViews.ViewSignatureFrom(derivedType,
                                                     baseDeclaringType,
                                                     baseOriginalSignature);
auto decision = overrides.CheckOverride(baseView, derivedSignature);

// Usage: overload candidate keeps both identities
AddOverloadCandidate(/*view*/ baseView,
                     /*original*/ baseOriginalSignature);</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

