---

## When method implementation resolution is needed

Method implementation resolution is needed for:

- class/interface validation before reporting `ESE0187` interface method collisions;
- selecting the effective default method inherited from a subinterface that overrides a superinterface default;
- deciding whether a superclass-selected default continues to satisfy a subclass requirement;
- avoiding verifier/class-linker failures from multiple emitted default implementations;
- runtime dispatch through interface references when no concrete class method exists;
- generic interface defaults after substitution.

The resolver should be invoked before lowering/emission commits to a default-method representation. A class should expose either a concrete implementation, one selected interface default, or a checker diagnostic; it should not rely on the verifier to discover unresolved default conflicts.

---

## Service dependency rules

The relation services should have an acyclic dependency order:

```text
GenericViewResolver
    -> OverrideOracle
        -> MethodImplementationResolver
        -> bridge/default emission planners

GenericViewResolver
    -> OverloadSetOracle
        -> call resolution
```

Rules:

- `GenericViewResolver` is the lowest-level helper for substituted views.
- `OverrideOracle` may consume `GenericViewResolver`.
- `OverloadSetOracle` may consume `GenericViewResolver` and `OverrideOracle` for inherited candidate suppression.
- `MethodImplementationResolver` may consume `GenericViewResolver` and `OverrideOracle` for default dominance.
- `OverrideOracle` must not depend on `OverloadSetOracle` or `MethodImplementationResolver`; otherwise lazy caches can form cycles.
- Bridge/default emission planning consumes semantic decisions; it must not rediscover override/default semantics.

---

## Cache layers to consider

## Inherited method candidate cache

```cpp
struct InheritedMethodKey {
    ETSObjectType *type;
    util::StringView name;
    MethodSearchKind kind;
};
```

Value:

```cpp
ArenaVector<InheritedMethodCandidate>
```

This avoids repeatedly traversing superclass/interface hierarchies and redoing substitutions.

## Override pair cache

```cpp
struct OverrideKey {
    MethodTargetKey base;
    MethodTargetKey derived;
    TypeRelationFlag flags;
};
```

