Introduce a checker-owned manager:

```cpp
class SemanticRelationCache {
public:
    explicit SemanticRelationCache(ETSChecker *checker);

    void Clear();

    OverrideOracle &Overrides();
    OverloadSetOracle &Overloads();
    MethodImplementationResolver &Implementations();
    GenericViewResolver &GenericViews();

private:
    ETSChecker *checker_ {};
    OverrideOracle overrideOracle_;
    OverloadSetOracle overloadOracle_;
    MethodImplementationResolver implementationResolver_;
    GenericViewResolver genericViewResolver_;
};
```

In the short-term design, cache correctness comes from strict clearing at `Recheck` and plugin mutation barriers. An epoch/generation counter is optional: useful as a debug guard or later for fine-grained LSP/plugin incremental invalidation, but not required if caches are never reused across those barriers.

