Responsibilities:

- build free-function overload sets from scope declarations;
- build instance-method overload sets in spec order: own candidates, direct superclass set, direct interface sets in `implements` order;
- build interface-method overload sets in spec order: own candidates, direct superinterface sets in `extends` order;
- build static-method overload sets from directly declared static methods only;
- build constructor overload sets, including anonymous constructors and explicit named constructor overloads;
- expand listed names in explicit overload declarations, including names that denote implicit overload groups;
- use `OverrideOracle` queries to skip inherited candidates already represented by overriding methods;
- preserve candidate declaration/listing order for first-match overload resolution.

Overload sets should generally be lazy because most possible member-name/type combinations are never used. A call expression asks for one overload set, validates candidates against its arguments, and stores the selected target. The cache is discarded on `Recheck` or plugin mutation barriers.

`OverloadSetOracle` caches declaration/candidate lists only. It must not cache call-specific generic inference results unless the key explicitly includes argument types, explicit type arguments, contextual type, and inference constraints.

