content.text:
Overload sets are needed for:

- function calls;
- method calls;
- constructor calls;
- explicit overload declaration validation;
- method/function references;
- `typeof` on overloaded names;
- explicit overload lowering;
- overload-set warnings.

Overload sets should usually be computed lazily:

```cpp
const auto &set = checker->SemanticRelations().Overloads().GetOverloadSet({
    .receiverType = receiverType,
    .name = methodName,
    .kind = OverloadSetKind::INSTANCE_METHOD,
});
```

The cache is valid only until the next `Recheck` or plugin cache clear.

