content.text:
- getter/setter pairs must remain distinguishable from ordinary methods;
- optional interface properties and generated accessors must be represented as accessor views or explicitly kept out of method implementation resolution with a separate property resolver.

### MethodView filtering rules

`EffectiveInstanceMethodViews(type)` must be defined precisely. For override/default validation it should include:

- own declared instance methods/accessors;
- inherited superclass methods that remain visible/effective in the current class view;
- selected inherited default implementations represented by `MethodImplementationResolver` when they satisfy interface requirements.

It should exclude:

- static methods;
- private superinterface defaults from public implementation/default resolution;
- private superclass methods that are not accessible override candidates;
- synthetic bridge/default-forwarder/helper methods generated after checking;
- explicit overload alias declarations, because aliases are not implementation bodies.

