```cpp
if (implementationResolver.HasCommonImplementation(classType, sigA, sigB)) {
    return; // no interface conflict; one implementation resolves both defaults
}
```

edits.newText:
Before reporting a conflict between two inherited interface default methods, validation must ask whether one implementation already resolves both requirements. This can be a convenience query on `SemanticRelations` backed by group-based implementation resolution:

```cpp
if (checker->SemanticRelations().HasCommonImplementation(classType, sigA, sigB)) {
    return; // no interface conflict; one implementation resolves both defaults
}
```

