content.text:
For constructors:

- unnamed constructors are implicitly overloaded in textual order;
- named constructors may be ordered by an explicit constructor overload;
- an anonymous constructor is placed first when explicit named constructor overloads exist.

## Type erasure and bridge methods

The spec defines effective types and effective signature types. These are needed for:

- overload-equivalence;
- erasure-related override diagnostics;
- bridge method necessity.

A bridge method is needed when a derived method overrides a base method, but the runtime/erased callable descriptor needed for dispatch differs from the real overriding method descriptor.

Bridge method requirements:

- synthetic/inaccessible from source;
- excluded from source overload sets;
- has base/effective callable descriptor;
- delegates to the real derived method;
- casts/converts arguments and return value as necessary.

