### Relation to current `AreOverrideCompatible`

The existing file-local helper in `checker/ets/object.cpp` is a useful seed:

```cpp
static bool AreOverrideCompatible(ETSChecker *checker, Signature *s1, Signature *s2)
{
    if (s1->Function()->Id()->Name() != s2->Function()->Id()->Name()) {
        return false;
    }

    SavedTypeRelationFlagsContext ctx(checker->Relation(), TypeRelationFlag::OVERRIDING_CONTEXT);
    return checker->Relation()->SignatureIsSupertypeOf(s1, s2);
}
```

It should not be treated as the final shared helper because:

- it is file-local and not the shared source of truth for checker, interface validation, overload suppression, and bridge planning;
- it is signature-only and assumes callers already produced the correct generic/substituted inherited view;
- the name sounds symmetric, but `SignatureIsSupertypeOf(s1, s2)` is directional;
- candidate filtering is outside the helper and therefore inconsistent across callers;
- it returns only `bool`, while diagnostics and characterization tests need a reason;
- related checks such as type-parameter compatibility and final/access/return diagnostics are split across other helpers.

The proposed helper should reuse the same `TypeRelation` core, but wrap it in a view-based, side-effect-free contract:

```cpp
enum class OverrideDecisionKind {
    OVERRIDES,
    NOT_SAME_NAME,
    NOT_CANDIDATE_KIND,
    INCOMPATIBLE_TYPE_PARAMS,
    INCOMPATIBLE_SIGNATURE,
};

struct OverrideDecision {
    OverrideDecisionKind kind;
    bool Overrides() const { return kind == OverrideDecisionKind::OVERRIDES; }
};

OverrideDecision CheckOverrideCompatibility(ETSChecker *checker,
                                            const MethodView &base,
                                            const MethodView &derived)
{
    if (base.key.name != derived.key.name) {
        return {OverrideDecisionKind::NOT_SAME_NAME};
    }

    if (!IsOverrideCandidatePair(base, derived)) {
        return {OverrideDecisionKind::NOT_CANDIDATE_KIND};
    }

    if (!HaveCompatibleMethodTypeParameters(checker, base, derived)) {
        return {OverrideDecisionKind::INCOMPATIBLE_TYPE_PARAMS};
    }

    SavedTypeRelationFlagsContext ctx(checker->Relation(), TypeRelationFlag::OVERRIDING_CONTEXT);
    if (!checker->Relation()->SignatureIsSupertypeOf(base.viewSignature, derived.viewSignature)) {
        return {OverrideDecisionKind::INCOMPATIBLE_SIGNATURE};
    }

    return {OverrideDecisionKind::OVERRIDES};
}

bool IsOverrideCompatible(ETSChecker *checker, const MethodView &base, const MethodView &derived)
{
    return CheckOverrideCompatibility(checker, base, derived).Overrides();
}
```

This helper must not emit diagnostics, mutate AST, call `SetOverride()`, or modify signatures. TypeRelation cache effects are acceptable.

Important query types:

- pair compatibility cache;

